 yet stocks have hit fresh records. Here\u2019s how long the defiance can last.", "feed": "MarketWatch Top", "ts": "2026-08-14T13:31:00+00:00", "url": "https://www.marketwatch.com/story/rates-are-at-multiyear-highs-yet-stocks-hit-fresh-records-heres-how-long-the-defiance-may-last-b29a5d14?mod=mw_rss_topstories", "status": "skipped", "excerpt": "", "citation": "Bond yields are at multiyear highs, yet stocks have hit fresh records. Here\u2019s how long the defiance can last. \u2014 MarketWatch Top, 2026-08-14. https://www.marketwatch.com/story/rates-are-at-multiyear-highs-yet-stocks-hit-fresh-records-heres-how-long-the-defiance-may-last-b29a5d14?mod=mw_rss_topstories"}, {"title": "AI-driven surge in bond yields could be next risk for markets and growth", "feed": "BusinessLine Mkts", "ts": "2026-08-14T05:23:10+00:00", "url": "https://www.thehindubusinessline.com/markets/ai-driven-surge-in-bond-yields-could-be-next-risk-for-markets-and-growth/article71344109.ece", "status": "ok", "excerpt": "Analysts say surge in borrowing by AI \u201chyperscalers\u201d has been a leading factor pushing up yields, as buyers demand higher returns to keep purchasing the flood \u200cof bonds hitting markets | Photo Credit: istock.com\n\nMarket gauges of inflation-adjusted borrowing costs \u200bhave shot to their highest in more than a decade across major economies as AI companies and governments ramp up bond sales, raising \u200crisks for stock markets and the world economy.\n\nReal yields are the returns that a bond investor demands above \u200binflation and are an important indicator of true borrowing costs for governments and companies. They are \u2060typically determined by expectations about growth, interest rates and the supply an", "citation": "AI-driven surge in bond yields could be next risk for markets and growth \u2014 BusinessLine Mkts, 2026-08-14. https://www.thehindubusinessline.com/markets/ai-driven-surge-in-bond-yields-could-be-next-risk-for-markets-and-growth/article71344109.ece"}, {"title": "Indian bonds poised for positive start on lower oil prices, Treasury yields", "feed": "BusinessLine Mkts", "ts": "2026-08-14T03:34:22+00:00", "url": "https://www.thehindubusinessline.com/markets/indian-bonds-poised-for-positive-start-on-lower-oil-prices-treasury-yields/article71343962.ece", "status": "ok", "excerpt": "New \u200cDelhi \u2060will raise \u20b9320 billion through \u2060a bond sale later in the day, including two new securities: a three-year and a seven-year paper. | Photo Credit: iStockphoto\n\nIndian government bonds are likely to witness positive momentum on \u200bFriday, supported by easing oil prices and lower US Treasury \u200cyields, although fresh supply from the weekly \u200bdebt auction could limit further advances.\n\nThe yield \u2060on the benchmark 6.94 per cent 2036 bond is expected to be in the 6.75 per cent to 6.78 per cent range ahead of \u200cthe auction, according to a trader at a private bank, after closing at 6.7582 per cent on \u200cThursday. Bond yields move inversely to prices.\n\nNew \u200cDelhi \u2060will raise \u20b9320 billion ($3.35 b", "citation": "Indian bonds poised for positive start on lower oil prices, Treasury yields \u2014 BusinessLine Mkts, 2026-08-14. https://www.thehindubusinessline.com/markets/indian-bonds-poised-for-positive-start-on-lower-oil-prices-treasury-yields/article71343962.ece"}], "primary_sources": [{"series": "ust_30y", "name": "FRED \u00b7 DGS30", "url": "https://fred.stlouisfed.org/series/DGS30"}, {"series": "ust_10y", "name": "FRED \u00b7 DGS10", "url": "https://fred.stlouisfed.org/series/DGS10"}, {"series": "tips_10y_real", "name": "FRED \u00b7 DFII10", "url": "https://fred.stlouisfed.org/series/DFII10"}], "analogues": {"member_z_today": {"ust_30y": 0.74, "ust_10y": 1.11, "tips_10y_real": 1.81}, "analogues": [{"date": "2026-05-22", "distance": 0.0, "member_z": {"ust_30y": 0.74, "ust_10y": 1.11, "tips_10y_real": 1.81}}, {"date": "2026-05-07", "distance": 0.25, "member_z": {"ust_